    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The core of the arguments generally focuses on how big tech platforms use their dominant market positions to unfairly favor their own services and stifle competition. Proponents of the investigations argue that these \"gatekeeper\" companies engage in anti-competitive self-preferencing and predatory tactics to lock out smaller rivals.\n\nSkeptics, on the other side, often argue that the large size and success of these companies are the *result* of superior innovation and benefit the consumer through lower prices and better services.\n\nThis debate really revolves around where the line is drawn between aggressive, successful competition and illegal monopolistic power.",
      "source": "target",
